# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env.
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT POINTS AT THE NEON `dev` BRANCH, NOT `production` (DEPLOY.md §2).
#
# `production` is the project's default branch and the real registry. An inn
# code claim is permanent — a retired
# code is never reissued (G3) and a market code is never reassigned (M7) — so a
# `npm run issue` typed at a laptop against `main` burns a code in the system of
# record with no undo. The dev branch exists so that mistake costs nothing.
#
# Create it with auto-delete set to Never — the Neon dialog defaults to a short
# expiry meant for throwaway preview branches.
#
# Two URLs because Neon pools connections: DATABASE_URL is the pooled endpoint
# the app runs on, DIRECT_URL the non-pooled one Prisma needs for migrations.
# Same split Inspire uses (mhotels-inspire/DEPLOY.md).
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST-pooler/neondb?sslmode=require"
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/neondb?sslmode=require"

# Local development against a throwaway Postgres, e.g.:
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres@localhost:5432/console_dev"
# DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres@localhost:5432/console_dev"
#
# `npm run verify:constraints` refuses anything that is not a local
# `*_test`/`*_dev` database, because it drops every registry table. The Neon dev
# branch is still called `neondb`, so that guard refuses it too — deliberately.

# Signs the session cookie. 32+ characters; rotating it signs everyone out.
# Production has its OWN value, set in Vercel — sessions should not cross.
#   openssl rand -base64 48
AUTH_SECRET=""

# ── Vercel only ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not needed locally: your SSH key already reaches the private repo.
#
# Read-only, fine-grained GitHub token scoped to imazanka-mcx/mhg-icgenerator.
# scripts/vercel-install.sh uses it to clone @mcx/inn-code over HTTPS. See
# DEPLOY.md §3.
# INN_CODE_TOKEN=""
